{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-03T09:25:58.030Z","data":{"text":"Task 9 complete.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- **`src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts`**: `InboxDispatchOptions` now extends `CommandInputs`; `inboxDispatchCommand` uses `resolveInputs` and `inputs.config()`. Text/JSON views write `text + \"\\n\"` through the resolved `stdout`. Card session and follow loop always receive resolved `stdout`/`stderr`. Both wait recorders get a `stderr` seam that appends `\\n`. The default sound uses `createInboxSound`'s `bell`/`warn` seams so the bell goes to `stdout` and warnings to `stderr`; a passed `sound` is untouched. Removed `console.*` fallbacks.\n- **`src/cli/inbox-terminal.ts`**: `createTerminalInput(stream, stdout = processStdout)` writes the `line` question through the writer.\n- **`tests/inbox-cards.test.ts` / `tests/inbox-dispatch.test.ts`**: expect the new trailing newline; the terminal line test asserts the question reaches its writer.\n- **`tests/command-inputs-inbox.test.ts`** (new): compares `runCli` vs. direct calls for `osq inbox` and `osq inbox --json`, and asserts the wait-log failure line and the default bell reach passed writers.\n\nBoth `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/command-inputs-inbox.test.ts` and `pnpm verify` exit 0. Result written to `openspec/changes/142-command-inputs/.run/results/9.md`."}}
